  "title": "OEIS A326097: the parity of a(k) (Hanna's conjecture)",
  "abstract": "The e.g.f. A(x) of OEIS A326097 satisfies 1 = Σ_{n≥0} ((1+x)^n − A(x))^n/n!. The package proves that this equation has exactly one solution in ℚ[[x]], that every a(k) = k! [x^k] A(x) is an integer, and that a(k) is odd if and only if k ∈ {0, 1, 3} or k ≡ 2 (mod 4). This settles Paul D. Hanna's 2019 parity conjecture in a slightly stronger form. The same holds for OEIS A385907, where (1+x)^n is replaced by 1/(1−x)^n.",
